.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_CTX_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_new ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_dup ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_free ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_CTX_is_a
.Nd public key algorithm context functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft EVP_PKEY_CTX *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_new
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "ENGINE *e"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_PKEY_CTX *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id
.Fa "int id"
.Fa "ENGINE *e"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_PKEY_CTX *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *name"
.Fa "const char *propquery"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_PKEY_CTX *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "const char *propquery"
.Fc
.Ft EVP_PKEY_CTX *
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_dup
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_free
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_CTX_is_a
.Fa "EVP_PKEY_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *keytype"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new
function allocates public key algorithm context using the
.Fa pkey
key type and ENGINE
.Fa e .
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id
function allocates public key algorithm context using the key type
specified by
.Fa id
and ENGINE
.Fa e .
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name
function allocates a public key algorithm context using the library
context
.Fa libctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 Ns ),
the key type specified by
.Fa name
and the property query
.Fa propquery .
None of the arguments are duplicated, so they must remain unchanged for
the lifetime of the returned
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
or of any of its duplicates.
Read further about the possible names in
.Sx NOTES
below.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey
function allocates a public key algorithm context using the library
context
.Fa libctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 )
and the algorithm specified by
.Fa pkey
and the property query
.Fa propquery .
None of the arguments are duplicated, so they must remain unchanged for
the lifetime of the returned
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
or any of its duplicates.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name
are normally used when no
.Vt EVP_PKEY
structure is associated with the operations, for example during
parameter generation or key generation for some algorithms.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_dup
duplicates the context
.Fa ctx .
It is not supported for a keygen operation.
It is however possible to duplicate a context freshly created via any of
the above
.Qo Li new Qc
functions, provided
.Xr EVP_PKEY_keygen_init 3
has not yet been called on the source context, and then use the copy for
key generation.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_free
frees up the context
.Fa ctx .
If
.Fa ctx
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Xr EVP_PKEY_is_a 3
checks if the key type associated with
.Fa ctx
is
.Fa keytype .
.Sh NOTES
.Ss \&OnEVP_PKEY_CTX
The
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
structure is an opaque public key algorithm context used by the OpenSSL
high-level public key API. Contexts
.Sy MUST NOT
be shared between threads: that is it is not permissible to use the same
context simultaneously in two threads.
.Ss \&On Key Types
We mention "key type" in this manual, which is the same as "algorithm"
in most cases, allowing either term to be used interchangeably.
There are algorithms where the
.Em key type
and the
.Em algorithm
of the operations that use the keys are not the same, such as EC keys
being used for ECDSA and ECDH operations.
.Pp
Key types are given in two different manners:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Legacy NID or EVP_PKEY type
This is the
.Fa id
used with
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id .
.Pp
These are
.Sy EVP_PKEY_RSA ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_RSA_PSS ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_DSA ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_DH ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_EC ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_SM2 ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_X25519 ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_X448 ,
and are used by legacy methods.
.It Name strings
This is the
.Fa name
used with
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name .
.Pp
These are names like "RSA", "DSA", and what's available depends on what
providers are currently accessible.
.Pp
The OpenSSL providers offer a set of key types available this way,
please see
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-FIPS 7
and
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-default 7
and related documentation for more information.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_dup
return either the newly allocated
.Vt EVP_PKEY_CTX
structure or
.Dv NULL
if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_free
does not return a value.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_is_a
returns 1 for true and 0 for false.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_new 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_id ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_dup
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_free
functions were added in OpenSSL 1.0.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_pkey
functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
